{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>A wild ass of a man</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 16:12): he loves the wildernesses to hunt animals, as it is written (Genesis 21:20), \"And he dwelt in the wilderness and became an archer.\" \"His hand against everyone\" — bandits. \"And everyone's hand against him\" — everyone hates him and makes war against him. But the correct interpretation is that \"פֶּרֶא אָדָם\" is in the construct state, meaning he will be a man like a wild ass, trained in the wilderness; he goes out in his activity seeking prey, and he tears all apart and all tear him apart. The matter concerns his seed, that they will multiply and have wars with all the nations. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 16:12): \"His hand against everyone\" — that he will first defeat all the nations, and afterward \"everyone's hand against him\" — that he will be defeated in the end; \"before all his brothers\" — who are the sons of Keturah — \"he shall dwell\" — that his seed will multiply from them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:03.821277774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}